    {
      "id": "ZyNjt9ueQ6dN4mYYgruWL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1210.3229377075202,
      "y": 1902.2671361061848,
      "width": 904.439453125,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1236375710,
      "version": 1462,
      "versionNonce": 1972608632,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789809573241,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Dictionaries are the most widely used in-built data type as far as i know.\nDictionaries carry key:value pair.\n\nDICTIONARIES DONT ALLOW DUPLICATE KEYS.\n\n-> Define Dictionary \n\ncustomer = {\n    \"name\" : \"john smith\",\n    \"age\" : 30\n    \"is_verified\" : True\n}\n\n-> Access a key (printing value)\n\nprint(customer[\"name\"]) #will print \"john smith\"\n\n#This sometimes gives error when key not present. Therefore, we use get method\n\n-> Get method \n\nprint(customer.get(\"name\"))\n\n#Why do we avoid error? because errors cause you to stop the program , that is very \nnot feasible innit? so even if a key doesnt exist it doesnt throw an error it still keeps the \nprogram running.\n\n-> default value assignment for non existing keys\neg : print(customer.get(\"birthday\",\"Jan 1 2006\")) #Since the dict doesnt have  birthday key \n#It prints \"Jan 1 2006\" instead. \n\n-> Update a value \n\ncustomer[\"name\"] = \"Jack Smith\"\n\nif we print(customer.get(\"name\")) # we get Jack Smith\n\n-> Add a new key:value pair in the dict\ncustomer[\"birthday\"] = \"Jan 1 2006\"\n\nadds => \"birthday\" : \"Jan 1 2006\" To the dictionary",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Dictionaries are the most widely used in-built data type as far as i know.\nDictionaries carry key:value pair.\n\nDICTIONARIES DONT ALLOW DUPLICATE KEYS.\n\n-> Define Dictionary \n\ncustomer = {\n    \"name\" : \"john smith\",\n    \"age\" : 30\n    \"is_verified\" : True\n}\n\n-> Access a key (printing value)\n\nprint(customer[\"name\"]) #will print \"john smith\"\n\n#This sometimes gives error when key not present. Therefore, we use get method\n\n-> Get method \n\nprint(customer.get(\"name\"))\n\n#Why do we avoid error? because errors cause you to stop the program , that is very \nnot feasible innit? so even if a key doesnt exist it doesnt throw an error it still keeps the \nprogram running.\n\n-> default value assignment for non existing keys\neg : print(customer.get(\"birthday\",\"Jan 1 2006\")) #Since the dict doesnt have  birthday key \n#It prints \"Jan 1 2006\" instead. \n\n-> Update a value \n\ncustomer[\"name\"] = \"Jack Smith\"\n\nif we print(customer.get(\"name\")) # we get Jack Smith\n\n-> Add a new key:value pair in the dict\ncustomer[\"birthday\"] = \"Jan 1 2006\"\n\nadds => \"birthday\" : \"Jan 1 2006\" To the dictionary",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
