      "text": "#Suppose Tyrion was 5 feet but the class said no he cant be; lets write \nthis in code.\n\nclass tyrionlanister():\n    name = \"tyrion lanister\"\n    height = \"3 feet\"\n\n#Now tyrion says no i am 5 feet , but the class says otherwise\n\ntyrion = tyrionlanister()\ntyrion.height = \"5 feet\" \n\nprint(tyrion.name , tyrion.height)\n\n#So what should be printed? 3 feet or 5 feet?\n\n#The answer is 5 feet ,Because python says instance object has\nmore value than of class object During assignment or retrieval.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "#Suppose Tyrion was 5 feet but the class said no he cant be; lets write \nthis in code.\n\nclass tyrionlanister():\n    name = \"tyrion lanister\"\n    height = \"3 feet\"\n\n#Now tyrion says no i am 5 feet , but the class says otherwise\n\ntyrion = tyrionlanister()\ntyrion.height = \"5 feet\" \n\nprint(tyrion.name , tyrion.height)\n\n#So what should be printed? 3 feet or 5 feet?\n\n#The answer is 5 feet ,Because python says instance object has\nmore value than of class object During assignment or retrieval.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "-tzlEgciM08BYWpNX2W3n",
