    },
    {
      "id": "D-rMBTcKOk1zn4MQ7CcDi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2028.7844924310307,
      "y": 3259.6399389432945,
      "width": 596.11962890625,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 32885950,
      "version": 869,
      "versionNonce": 1733013112,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "kmBjFP_zphenZFjohsTkh",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789809573241,
      "created": 1789641750523,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So what are methods? \n-> Methods can be called the functions that can be used on \nany object created from their corresponding class.\n\nHow do we create method? (They are functions i told ya)\n\nclass Employee():\n    role = \"Backend Engineer\"\n    salary = 4000000\n\ndef getInfo(self): \n    print(f\"{self.name} {self.role} {self.salary}\")\n\nishaan = Employee()\n\nishaan.name = \"Ishaan Chavan\"\n\ngetInfo(ishaan)\n\n \n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So what are methods? \n-> Methods can be called the functions that can be used on \nany object created from their corresponding class.\n\nHow do we create method? (They are functions i told ya)\n\nclass Employee():\n    role = \"Backend Engineer\"\n    salary = 4000000\n\ndef getInfo(self): \n    print(f\"{self.name} {self.role} {self.salary}\")\n\nishaan = Employee()\n\nishaan.name = \"Ishaan Chavan\"\n\ngetInfo(ishaan)\n\n \n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
