      "text": "Staticmethod (@staticmethod) :",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Staticmethod (@staticmethod) :",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LRIVMOHBFkH-cCqNKuA8W",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2024.9248221693597,
      "y": 3812.9048774394682,
      "width": 555.479736328125,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1f",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2022225918,
      "version": 742,
      "versionNonce": 1423418232,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "ZTalIrnyeBTT7k-hOLkp6",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1789809573241,
      "created": 1789642918571,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Staticmethod is a decorator(we will come to this later)\n\nwhat does static method do? \n-> It allows a method to run without an object passed \nthrough it.\n\n-> imagine a method greetUser():\n\nis it necessary to pass self(the whole object) to \njust greet the user? \n\nNo right? \n\n-> so assume :\n\nclass Employee():\n    role = \"Backend Engineer\"\n    salary = 4000000\n\n@staticmethod \ndef greetUser(): #does it need to know role, salary?? No\n    print(\"Good Morning\")\n\nishaan = Employee()\n\nishaan.name = \"Ishaan Chavan\"\n\ngreetUser()",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Staticmethod is a decorator(we will come to this later)\n\nwhat does static method do? \n-> It allows a method to run without an object passed \nthrough it.\n\n-> imagine a method greetUser():\n\nis it necessary to pass self(the whole object) to \njust greet the user? \n\nNo right? \n\n-> so assume :\n\nclass Employee():\n    role = \"Backend Engineer\"\n    salary = 4000000\n\n@staticmethod \ndef greetUser(): #does it need to know role, salary?? No\n    print(\"Good Morning\")\n\nishaan = Employee()\n\nishaan.name = \"Ishaan Chavan\"\n\ngreetUser()",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
