    {
      "id": "2-9VfAItLDPMV3kCl3y4r",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2689.215371090813,
      "y": 3888.4865943875902,
      "width": 678.279541015625,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1808648418,
      "version": 254,
      "versionNonce": 777762424,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789809573241,
      "created": 1789645120989,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Constructor (__init__ method) (__init__ is also a dunder method) : ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Constructor (__init__ method) (__init__ is also a dunder method) : ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "om5doXm-E79VSPMZ92Hoi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2721.5110508649504,
      "y": 3941.86771154362,
      "width": 607.5396728515625,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 460912254,
      "version": 820,
      "versionNonce": 1060834568,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789809573241,
      "created": 1789645180076,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> __init__ is a method that is called w/o calling whenever an\nobject is created. \n\nHow do we define this method? \n\nclass Employee():\n\n    def __init__(self,name,salary,language):\n        self.name = name\n        self.salary = salary\n        self.language = language\n\nNow we dont need to make instance attribute like this for eg:\n\nishaan.name = \"Ishaan Chavan\"\n\nwe can define the name,salary,language for our employee when \ncreating an object\n\nishaan = Employee(\"ishaan\",2400000,\"Python\")\n\n#and we can print \n\nprint(ishaan.name , ishaan.salary , ishaan.language)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> __init__ is a method that is called w/o calling whenever an\nobject is created. \n\nHow do we define this method? \n\nclass Employee():\n\n    def __init__(self,name,salary,language):\n        self.name = name\n        self.salary = salary\n        self.language = language\n\nNow we dont need to make instance attribute like this for eg:\n\nishaan.name = \"Ishaan Chavan\"\n\nwe can define the name,salary,language for our employee when \ncreating an object\n\nishaan = Employee(\"ishaan\",2400000,\"Python\")\n\n#and we can print \n\nprint(ishaan.name , ishaan.salary , ishaan.language)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
