    },
    {
      "id": "ftGXWErDz5Q4vOCXQqq0F",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 238.4939571473168,
      "y": 5066.724570695325,
      "width": 562.2396240234375,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 380627134,
      "version": 150,
      "versionNonce": 1630847608,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789809573241,
      "created": 1789649118475,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Super method is used to access methods of parent class.\n\n-> how to use it? \n\nsuper().__init__(argument)\n\neg: \n\nclass Parent:\n    def __init__(self, name):\n        self.name = name\n\nclass Child(Parent):\n    def __init__(self, name, age):\n        super().__init__(name)  # Calls Parent's __init__\n        self.age = age   ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Super method is used to access methods of parent class.\n\n-> how to use it? \n\nsuper().__init__(argument)\n\neg: \n\nclass Parent:\n    def __init__(self, name):\n        self.name = name\n\nclass Child(Parent):\n    def __init__(self, name, age):\n        super().__init__(name)  # Calls Parent's __init__\n        self.age = age   ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "azGBAjzV18yCwNVZa5vEa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 986.6936876795183,
